m to backtrack  if they decide that you know he's not  really going to be doing this the one  time that kamala harris overstepped and  said that he is going to be running her  office had to step back the statement  the next day uh well now we're hearing  from democratic representative carolyn  maloney who represents part of new york  city that off the record joe biden is  not running for president again baloney  was speaking to the new york times  editorial board and the exchange went  like this new york times's eleanor  randolph said quote should president  biden run again maloney said off the  record he's not running again new york  times is joyouti thoughtman definitely  mispronouncing that said not off the  record on the record maloney said on the  record no he should not run again so  there was a bit of confusion about this  on the record versus off the record  thing both the reporter and the  interviewee are supposed to confirm and  agree that something is off the record  before it's truly off the record which  you can see didn't happen here in this  exchange but her position sure sounded  like biden won't be running again for a  second term she also doesn't want him to  run again as to why maloney might not  want biden to run again that's probably  because of his sagging approval numbers  they haven't been doing all that well in  in recent months although it has ticked  up a little bit over the past couple of  weeks he's back to around 40  but maybe maloney just sees biden as a  liability for the democrats and she  wants him to step aside and to get a new  face in there maloney later went on cnn  to apologize for the statement and to  say that biden's a great president and  she doesn't think that biden's going to  run again but she sure wants him to mr  president i apologize i want you to run  i happen to think you won't be running  but when you run or if you run i will be  there 100 percent you have deserved it  you are a great president and  thank you for e